{
  "about": "The comments an element owns, read by both readers from the same text and held to one table (graph spec §26 notes, §27 tagged comments). A run of /// note lines and //@ key: value lines is owned by the element on the line directly below it; a blank line or any other comment ends the run, and a line holding more than one element owns nothing. A //@ line with no key is an ordinary comment. Each case gives the block and what is owned (line of the element, the element, its tags in order, its note lines and its summary), the comment lines that own nothing, and the //@ lines that are malformed. Roger, 11 Oct 2026: /// and //@ lines mix in one run, and a //@ line is never a note. A case with \"refused\" gives the line both readers refuse it at instead. A case with \"notes\" also gives what notes() reads (editor spec §24): each note with its element's line, the element, its /// lines, its text (those lines joined, CommonMark for the host to render) and its summary; and, in \"shared\", each line holding more than one element with a note above it, which belongs to none of them. Each case has a stable id, and names the requirements it proves: req:26 and req:27 are the graph spec's, plain ids such as note_comment the editor's (\"partial\" where it proves part).",
